      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:1:31:3",
      "text": [
        " سُئِلَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الرَّجُلِ يُطَلِّقُ امْرَأَتَهُ وَ بَيْنَهُمَا وَلَدٌ أَيُّهُمَا أَحَقُّ بِالْوَلَدِ قَالَ الْمَرْأَةُ أَحَقُّ بِالْوَلَدِ مَا لَمْ تَتَزَوَّجْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from Ali Bin Muhammad Al Qasany, from Al Qasim Bin Muhammad, from Al Minqary, from the one who mentioned it, said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> was asked about the man who divorces his wife, and between the two of them is a child, which of the two is more rightful with the child?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The woman is more rightful with the child so long as she does not get married (again)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from Ali ibn Muhammad al-Qasaniy from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from al-Minqariy from those whom he has mentioned who has said the following: “Once, abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, was asked about the case of a man who divorces his wife. They have a child, which one of them has more right for the child? He (the Imam) said, ‘The woman has more right as long as she does not marry.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
